        A V100 and D V100 share one register description (one data sheet). The A V200 and 3519 V101 use the same block types (the _AV200 ISP/VICAP/MIPI/VDP editions, MDDRC, FMC, PERI_CRG, MUX/PAD). The A V300 and D V300 are the next generation: DMAC_V2, I2C_V2, FEMAC, LSADC_V2, SPACC/RSA/OTP_USER, VEDU_V3 and the _AV300 editions; the D V300 root uses chip-local blocks extracted from its own data sheet where the A V300 root has shared editions or none (VICAP, VDP and CRG/MISC_CTRL registers are identical to the A V300 ones: docs/rdl-campaign/hi3516dv300-compare.md). Blocks that are absent in a column are absent from that root (not necessarily from the chip; see block-presence.csv).

